.ds n) ucsdpsys_turtleserver
.TH \*(n) 1 ucsd-psystem-vm "Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
ucsdpsys_turtleserver \- Turtle Graphics server
.XX "ucsdpsys_turtleserver(1)" "Turtle Graphics server"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B \*(n)
.br
.B \*(n)
.B -V
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fI\*(n)\fP program is used by the \f[I]ucsdpsys_vm\fP(1) program to
draw graphics, via the specially crafted TURTLEGRAPHICS unit.
This command is not usually invoked directly by the user.
.PP
When \f[I]ucsdpsys_vm\fP(1) uses a terminal for its console (rather
than its own SDL3 window, which shows Turtle Graphics itself), it starts
this program the first time a program calls the TURTLEGRAPHICS unit, sends it one command per line on its
standard input, and reads replies from its standard output.
.PP
The 280\(mu192 picture is shown in a window, drawn with SDL3.
INITTURTLE and GRAFMODE show the window; TEXTMODE hides it.
Closing the window only hides it.
Without a graphics display, drawing continues off screen, so programs
that read the screen back (SCREENBIT) still work.
.br
.ne 1i
.SH OPTIONS
The following options are understood:
.TP 8n
\fB\-V\fP
Print the version of the
.I \*(n)
program being executed.
.PP
All other options will produce a diagnostic error.
.so man/man1/z_exit.so
